---
import BaseLayout from '../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Let's compare notes"
  description="An invitation to compare notes on how organisations turn research, customer insight and internal expertise into ideas that influence decisions."
>
  <header class="compare-hero">
    <div class="container-site compare-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="t-label mb-6">An open research invitation</p>
        <h1 class="t-display mb-6">Let's compare notes</h1>
        <p class="compare-question">
          How do organisations turn research, customer insight and internal expertise into ideas that actually influence decisions?
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="compare-intro">
        <p>
          Over the past year, I've been developing what I call Editorial Intelligence — a way of thinking about how evidence becomes narrative, and how narrative becomes organisational knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Much of that thinking has come from my work in B2B technology and enterprise software. Now I'd like to test it beyond that environment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="container-site compare-section">
      <div class="compare-section-heading">
        <p class="t-label">Who I'd like to hear from</p>
        <h2>People responsible for turning expertise into something useful</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="people-grid" role="list">
        {[
          'Content leaders',
          'Editorial teams',
          'Product marketers',
          'Research teams',
          'Consultants',
          'Founders',
        ].map((person, index) => (
          <div class="person-item" role="listitem">
            <span class="person-num">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span>{person}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="people-note">
        The job title matters less than the responsibility. If part of your work involves turning knowledge, evidence or expertise into content, I'd be interested in your perspective.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider container-site" />

    <section class="container-site compare-section questions-section">
      <div class="questions-intro">
        <p class="t-label mb-5">What we could discuss</p>
        <h2>I'm looking for honest conversations</h2>
        <p>
          I'm not selling anything through these conversations. I want to understand where the work breaks down, what has changed and what still feels harder than it should.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="question-list">
        {[
          'What is the hardest part of creating thought leadership?',
          'Where does valuable knowledge get lost?',
          'Has AI changed the way your team works?',
          'What still feels harder than it should?',
        ].map((question, index) => (
          <div class="question-item">
            <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <p>{question}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="learning-section">
      <div class="container-site learning-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="t-label mb-5">What I'm hoping to learn</p>
          <h2>A useful idea should survive contact with other people's work</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="learning-list">
          <li>Does Editorial Intelligence describe a problem you already recognise?</li>
          <li>Which parts resonate most — and which don't?</li>
          <li>Where does it overlap with existing roles or disciplines?</li>
          <li>What would make it genuinely useful in your organisation?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container-site compare-section">
      <div class="compare-section-heading">
        <p class="t-label">Ways to take part</p>
        <h2>Contribute in whichever way suits you</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="routes-grid" role="list">
        <div class="route-card" role="listitem">
          <span class="person-num">01</span>
          <h3>A 30-minute conversation</h3>
          <p>A video call comparing how evidence becomes influence in your organisation. Not an interview with a script — a genuine exchange between practitioners.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="route-card" role="listitem">
          <span class="person-num">02</span>
          <h3>The written questionnaire</h3>
          <p>Around 10–15 minutes, in your own time. It asks you to reconstruct one real example of evidence shaping a decision, then covers where knowledge gets lost and how AI is changing the work.</p>
          <a href="/compare-notes/questionnaire" class="route-link">
            Open the questionnaire
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <p class="route-pilot-tag">Pilot version 1</p>
        </div>
        <div class="route-card" role="listitem">
          <span class="person-num">03</span>
          <h3>An anonymous contribution</h3>
          <p>You can respond to the written questions without your name or organisation being recorded in the research at all. The questionnaire's contact fields are all optional — leave them blank and the response stays anonymous.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="people-note">
        The questionnaire is being piloted, so its wording may still change. Responses collected during the pilot remain part of the research, and any substantial revision is recorded so findings can be traced to the version that produced them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section">
      <div class="container-site">
        <div class="compare-section-heading terms-heading">
          <p class="t-label">How this works</p>
          <h2>What happens to what you share</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="terms-grid">
          <div class="terms-item">
            <h3>How your contribution is used</h3>
            <p>Contributions become part of the research evidence base behind Editorial Intelligence. They are synthesised — alongside other conversations and responses — into published findings, methodology improvements and, eventually, a first research report. Your contribution is analysed on the terms you choose: analysis only, anonymous use in findings, or available for attribution.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="terms-item">
            <h3>Attribution is optional — and off by default</h3>
            <p>Nothing is attributed to you or your organisation unless you separately approve the exact wording and context first. Your contact details stay in a private research tracker; they are never published and never added to a marketing list.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="terms-item">
            <h3>What you receive</h3>
            <p>This is an exchange, not an extraction. Participants receive the early synthesis of findings, anything from the methodology that's relevant to the problem they described, and — if they want it — a note when the research is published.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="terms-item">
            <h3>What happens after you get in touch</h3>
            <p>I reply personally — there's no automated sequence behind this page. We find a time or I send the questions, your contribution is logged as anonymised research evidence, and I follow up with something useful rather than a pitch. You can ask for your contribution to be withdrawn at any point before findings are aggregated.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="people-note">These are research conversations, not sales calls. If commercial work ever grows out of one, it will be because you raised it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container-site closing-section">
      <div class="closing-copy">
        <p>If my thinking is useful, brilliant.</p>
        <p>If it's wrong, I'd rather find out now than in three years' time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="closing-invite">
        <h2>Would you spend 30 minutes comparing notes?</h2>
        <p>Tell me a little about the work you do and the problem you keep encountering. We'll take it from there. If a conversation is harder to schedule, the questionnaire covers the same ground in your own time.</p>
        <div class="closing-actions">
          <a
            href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Let's%20compare%20notes&body=Hi%20Asavin%2C%0A%0AI'd%20be%20happy%20to%20compare%20notes.%20A%20little%20about%20my%20work%3A%0A%0A"
            class="compare-btn"
          >
            Start a conversation
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/compare-notes/questionnaire" class="compare-btn compare-btn-secondary">
            Answer the questionnaire
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ashwat/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="linkedin-link">
          Or message me on LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .compare-hero {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 11vw, 9rem) clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .compare-hero-grid,
  .learning-grid,
  .closing-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .compare-question {
    max-width: 25ch;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .compare-intro {
    align-self: end;
    max-width: 55ch;
  }

  .compare-intro p,
  .questions-intro > p:last-child,
  .closing-invite > p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .compare-intro p + p {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .compare-section {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .compare-section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .compare-section-heading h2,
  .questions-intro h2,
  .learning-grid h2,
  .closing-invite h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .compare-section-heading h2,
  .questions-intro h2,
  .learning-grid h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .people-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .person-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    min-height: 5rem;
    padding: 1.35rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .person-num,
  .question-item > span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
  }

  .people-note {
    max-width: 64ch;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
  }

  .questions-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .questions-intro {
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .questions-intro h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .question-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .question-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .question-item p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .learning-section {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    background: var(--color-surface-secondary);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .learning-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-surface-tertiary);
  }

  .learning-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.15rem 0 1.15rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-surface-tertiary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .learning-list li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .routes-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .route-card {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.35rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .route-card h3 {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .route-card p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .route-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .route-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .route-pilot-tag {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
  }

  .terms-section {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    background: var(--color-surface-secondary);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .terms-heading {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .terms-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--color-rule);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .terms-item {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.35rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .terms-item h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .terms-item p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .closing-section {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .closing-copy {
    align-self: center;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .closing-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .closing-invite {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background: var(--color-surface-secondary);
  }

  .closing-invite h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .closing-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .compare-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-surface);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.2s, opacity 0.2s;
  }

  .compare-btn:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .compare-btn-secondary {
    border-color: var(--color-rule);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .linkedin-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .linkedin-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .compare-hero-grid,
    .learning-grid,
    .closing-section {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    }

    .compare-section-heading {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.65fr) minmax(0, 1.35fr);
      align-items: start;
    }

    .people-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .questions-section {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
      gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    }

    .routes-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .terms-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .people-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .closing-actions {
      align-items: stretch;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .compare-btn {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
